 Art. 55 (M/46)  |  A fixed-term contract ends on expiry; if the parties continue to perform it, it is deemed renewed for an indefinite term, subject to Art. 37 for non-Saudis. If the contract contains a renewal clause for a similar or specified term, it renews for that term; if it is renewed three consecutive times, or the original term plus renewals reaches four years, whichever is less, and the parties continue to perform it, it becomes an indefinite-term contract  |  For **Saudi** workers: continued work after expiry without a renewal clause converts immediately to indefinite; with an auto-renewal clause, conversion happens after the third consecutive renewal or four years' total term, whichever is earlier, plus continued performance. For **non-Saudis** conversion never happens (Art. 37 and Regs Art. 12). The 2005 body says two renewals / three years; that is superseded. Conversion changes the exposure from Art. 77(2) (remaining term) to Art. 75 notice plus Art. 77(1)  |  `[settled — last confirmed 2026-09-04]` `[BOE — Arabic]` `[BOE — official English]` 
 Art. 61 (paras 4-6 M/44) and Art. 62  |  Employer duties: (1) no forced labor, no withholding wages without a judicial instrument, respectful treatment; (2) time off to exercise statutory rights without wage deduction; (3) facilitate officials' tasks; (4) refrain from anything that would nullify or weaken equal opportunity or treatment in employment and occupation, whether by exclusion, distinction or preference among applicants or workers on the basis of race, colour, gender, age, disability, marital status or any other form of discrimination; (5) provide appropriate housing or an appropriate cash allowance paid with the wage; (6) provide appropriate transport from residence to workplace or an appropriate cash allowance paid with the wage. A worker who reports ready for work and is prevented only by a cause attributable to the employer is entitled to wages for that period (Art. 62)  |  Since 19 February 2025 every worker (Saudi or not) must receive housing and transport or cash allowances; the Law sets no amount ("appropriate"). HRSD Regs Art. 21 applies the housing duty to the private and non-profit sectors and defines forced labor `[authority — HRSD]`. Because the allowances are paid "with the wage" they fall within the actual wage (Art. 2) for end-of-service award and compensation unless a court holds otherwise `[model knowledge — verify]`. Para (4) is the general anti-discrimination duty; there is no statutory damages formula for breach (penalties under Art. 229)  |  `[settled — last confirmed 2026-09-04]` `[BOE — Arabic]` `[BOE — official English]` `[authority — HRSD]` 
 Arts. 71, 72 (M/44), 73 (M/46)  |  No disciplinary penalty without first notifying the worker in writing of the charge, interrogating him, hearing his defence and recording this in minutes placed in his file; oral interrogation is allowed for minor violations punishable by warning or a fine not exceeding one day's wage, if minuted (Art. 71). The penalty decision must be notified in writing (registered mail to the file address if he refuses or is absent); the worker may object in writing to the competent department at the employer within 30 days (excluding official holidays) of notification; if the objection is rejected or not decided in writing within 15 days of filing, he may appeal to the Labor Courts within 30 days (excluding official holidays) from the rejection or the lapse of the 15 days, whichever is earlier (Art. 72). Fines must be recorded in a special register and may be spent only for the benefit of the establishment's workers, by the labor committee or, if none, with the Ministry's approval (Art. 73)  |  M/44 inserted a mandatory internal grievance step (30 days to object, 15 days for the employer to answer) before the Labor Court appeal. Investigation files must show: written charge, interview, defence, signed minutes. The pre-M/44 route (15 days direct to the dispute body) shown in the scraped body is superseded. Fines cannot be kept by the employer  |  `[settled — last confirmed 2026-09-04]` `[BOE — Arabic]` `[BOE — official English]` 

