The Article 88 outer limit does not extend an earlier ordinary payroll due date. Pay through an approved bank. Do not condition payment of undisputed entitlements on signing a release or completing an unquantified equipment-clearance process. The clearance-hold interpretation retains `[model knowledge — verify]`.  
`labor-law.md`, Arts. 88, 90; Regulations Annex 1 Arts. 15–17, Annex 5 cls. 11.9–11.10. `[settled — last confirmed 2026-09-04]`

**Grievance timetable.** Article 72 provides 30 days excluding official holidays to grieve, 15 days for the employer’s written response, then 30 days excluding official holidays from rejection or expiry of the response period, whichever is earlier. Assume a disciplinary decision is effectively notified on 2026-09-04; a later notification requires recalculation. `[review]`

The files do not expressly settle whether both Friday and Saturday are excluded as “official holidays” for this particular clock. `[no rule in ksa files — verify]` The two illustrative calendars are therefore:

